docker copy image from one machine to another

docker image ls
docker save -o copy.watchtower.tar containrrr/watchtower
docker save -o copy.shadowbox.tar quay.io/outline/shadowbox

then copy to another machine
docker load -i copy.shadowbox.tar
docker image ls

wget https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Jigsaw-Code/outline-server/master/src/server_manager/install_scripts/install_server.sh
mkdir /sys/fs/cgroup/systemd
mount -t cgroup -o none,name=systemd cgroup /sys/fs/cgroup/systemd
docker run -itd containrrr/watchtower --cleanup --label-enable --tlsverify
docker run -itd quay.io/outline/shadowbox:stable
bash install_server.sh
this will output a dict like {"apiUrl":..., "sha256":} and it will be stored in /opt/outline/access.txt

add key
on local
download Outline-Manager.AppImage not Outline-Client.AppImage from github
install shadowsocks-qt5
then run it on client, click "get started"
copy the dict message from server into it,
click "add key" then click the key and share it, pull down the share page you'll find
the ss key address, and copy it to others

Issue
1. root@Mars:~# docker run -itd containrrr/watchtower                                     
docker: Error response from daemon: cgroups: cgroup mountpoint does not exist: unknown.

solved:
mkdir /sys/fs/cgroup/systemd
mount -t cgroup -o none,name=systemd cgroup /sys/fs/cgroup/systemd
docker run -itd containrrr/watchtower --cleanup --label-enable --tlsverify

2. docker run -itd outline/shadowbox:latest --cleanup --label-enable --tlsverify
Unable to find image 'quay.io/outline/shadowbox:latest' locally
docker: Error response from daemon: manifest for quay.io/outline/shadowbox:latest not found: manifest unknown: manifest unknown.

solved: 
docker image ls, show that tag is stable
docker run -itd quay.io/outline/shadowbox:stable

